        "tool_use_id": "toolu_01HcpfCUPQ2PdHXeyjZzorSU",
        "type": "tool_result",
        "content": "     1→# PostHog Next.js Pages Router Example Project\n     2→\n     3→Repository: https://github.com/PostHog/examples\n     4→Path: basics/next-pages-router\n     5→\n     6→---\n     7→\n     8→## README.md\n     9→\n    10→# PostHog Next.js pages router example\n    11→\n    12→This is a [Next.js](https://nextjs.org) Pages Router example demonstrating PostHog integration with product analytics, session replay, feature flags, and error tracking.\n    13→\n    14→## Features\n    15→\n    16→- **Product Analytics**: Track user events and behaviors\n    17→- **Session Replay**: Record and replay user sessions\n    18→- **Error Tracking**: Capture and track errors\n    19→- **User Authentication**: Demo login system with PostHog user identification\n    20→- **Server-side & Client-side Tracking**: Examples of both tracking methods\n    21→- **Reverse Proxy**: PostHog ingestion through Next.js rewrites\n    22→\n    23→## Getting Started\n    24→\n    25→### 1. Install Dependencies\n    26→\n    27→```bash\n    28→npm install\n    29→# or\n    30→pnpm install\n    31→```\n    32→\n    33→### 2. Configure Environment Variables\n    34→\n    35→Create a `.env.local` file in the root directory:\n    36→\n    37→```bash\n    38→NEXT_PUBLIC_POSTHOG_KEY=your_posthog_project_api_key\n    39→NEXT_PUBLIC_POSTHOG_HOST=https://us.i.posthog.com\n    40→```\n    41→\n    42→Get your PostHog API key from your [PostHog project settings](https://app.posthog.com/project/settings).\n    43→\n    44→### 3. Run the Development Server\n    45→\n    46→```bash\n    47→npm run dev\n    48→# or\n    49→pnpm dev\n    50→```\n    51→\n    52→Open [http://localhost:3000](http://localhost:3000) with your browser to see the app.\n    53→\n    54→## Project Structure\n    55→\n    56→```\n    57→src/\n    58→├── components/\n    59→│   └── Header.tsx           # Navigation header with auth state\n    60→├── contexts/\n    61→│   └── AuthContext.tsx      # Authentication context with PostHog integration\n    62→├── lib/\n    63→│   └── posthog-server.ts    # Server-side PostHog client\n    64→├── pages/\n    65→│   ├── _app.tsx             # App wrapper with Auth provider\n    66→│   ├── _document.tsx        # Document wrapper\n    67→│   ├── index.tsx            # Home/Login page\n    68→│   ├── burrito.tsx          # Demo feature page with event tracking\n    69→│   ├── profile.tsx          # User profile with error tracking demo\n    70→│   └── api/\n    71→│       └── auth/\n    72→│           └── login.ts     # Login API with server-side tracking\n    73→└── styles/\n    74→    └── globals.css          # Global styles\n    75→\n    76→instrumentation-client.ts    # Client-side PostHog initialization\n    77→```\n    78→\n    79→## Key Integration Points\n    80→\n    81→### Client-side initialization (instrumentation-client.ts)\n    82→\n    83→```typescript\n    84→import posthog from \"posthog-js\"\n    85→\n    86→posthog.init(process.env.NEXT_PUBLIC_POSTHOG_KEY!, {\n    87→  api_host: \"/ingest\",\n    88→  ui_host: \"https://us.posthog.com\",\n    89→  defaults: '2025-05-24',\n    90→  capture_exceptions: true,\n    91→  debug: process.env.NODE_ENV === \"development\",\n    92→});\n    93→```\n    94→\n    95→### User identification (AuthContext.tsx)\n    96→\n    97→```typescript\n    98→posthog.identify(username, {\n    99→  username: username,\n   100→});\n   101→```\n   102→\n   103→### Event tracking (burrito.tsx)\n   104→\n   105→```typescript\n   106→posthog.capture('burrito_considered', {\n   107→  total_considerations: count,\n   108→  username: username,\n   109→});\n   110→```\n   111→\n   112→### Error tracking (profile.tsx)\n   113→\n   114→```typescript\n   115→posthog.captureException(error);\n   116→```\n   117→\n   118→### Server-side tracking (api/auth/login.ts)\n   119→\n   120→```typescript\n   121→const posthog = getPostHogClient();\n   122→posthog.capture({\n   123→  distinctId: username,\n   124→  event: 'server_login',\n   125→  properties: { ... }\n   126→});\n   127→```\n   128→\n   129→## Pages router differences from app router\n   130→\n   131→This example uses Next.js Pages Router instead of App Router. Key differences:\n   132→\n   133→1. **File-based routing**: Pages in `src/pages/` instead of `src/app/`\n   134→2. **_app.tsx**: Custom App component wraps all pages\n   135→3. **API Routes**: Located in `src/pages/api/`\n   136→4. **No 'use client'**: All pages are client-side by default\n   137→5. **useRouter**: From `next/router` instead of `next/navigation`\n   138→6. **Head component**: Using `next/head` for metadata instead of `metadata` export\n   139→\n   140→## Learn More\n   141→\n   142→- [PostHog Documentation](https://posthog.com/docs)\n   143→- [Next.js Pages Router Documentation](https://nextjs.org/docs/pages)\n   144→- [PostHog Next.js Integration Guide](https://posthog.com/docs/libraries/next-js)\n   145→\n   146→## Deploy on Vercel\n   147→\n   148→The easiest way to deploy your Next.js app is to use the [Vercel Platform](https://vercel.com/new).\n   149→\n   150→Check out the [Next.js deployment documentation](https://nextjs.org/docs/pages/building-your-application/deploying) for more details.\n   151→\n   152→---\n   153→\n   154→## instrumentation-client.ts\n   155→\n   156→```ts\n   157→import posthog from \"posthog-js\"\n   158→\n   159→posthog.init(process.env.NEXT_PUBLIC_POSTHOG_KEY!, {\n   160→  api_host: \"/ingest\",\n   161→  ui_host: \"https://us.posthog.com\",\n   162→  // Include the defaults option as required by PostHog\n   163→  defaults: '2025-05-24',\n   164→  // Enables capturing unhandled exceptions via Error Tracking\n   165→  capture_exceptions: true,\n   166→  // Turn on debug in development mode\n   167→  debug: process.env.NODE_ENV === \"development\",\n   168→});\n   169→\n   170→//IMPORTANT: Never combine this approach with other client-side PostHog initialization approaches, especially components like a PostHogProvider. instrumentation-client.ts is the correct solution for initializating client-side PostHog in Next.js 15.3+ apps.\n   171→```\n   172→\n   173→---\n   174→\n   175→## next.config.ts\n   176→\n   177→```ts\n   178→import type { NextConfig } from \"next\";\n   179→\n   180→const nextConfig: NextConfig = {\n   181→  /* config options here */\n   182→  reactStrictMode: true,\n   183→  async rewrites() {\n   184→    return [\n   185→      {\n   186→        source: \"/ingest/static/:path*\",\n   187→        destination: \"https://us-assets.i.posthog.com/static/:path*\",\n   188→      },\n   189→      {\n   190→        source: \"/ingest/:path*\",\n   191→        destination: \"https://us.i.posthog.com/:path*\",\n   192→      },\n   193→    ];\n   194→  },\n   195→  // This is required to support PostHog trailing slash API requests\n   196→  skipTrailingSlashRedirect: true,\n   197→};\n   198→\n   199→export default nextConfig;\n   200→\n   201→```\n   202→\n   203→---\n   204→\n   205→## src/components/Header.tsx\n   206→\n   207→```tsx\n   208→import Link from 'next/link';\n   209→import { useAuth } from '@/contexts/AuthContext';\n   210→\n   211→export default function Header() {\n   212→  const { user, logout } = useAuth();\n   213→\n   214→  return (\n   215→    <header className=\"header\">\n   216→      <div className=\"header-container\">\n   217→        <nav>\n   218→          <Link href=\"/\">Home</Link>\n   219→          {user && (\n   220→            <>\n   221→              <Link href=\"/burrito\">Burrito Consideration</Link>\n   222→              <Link href=\"/profile\">Profile</Link>\n   223→            </>\n   224→          )}\n   225→        </nav>\n   226→        <div className=\"user-section\">\n   227→          {user ? (\n   228→            <>\n   229→              <span>Welcome, {user.username}!</span>\n   230→              <button onClick={logout} className=\"btn-logout\">\n   231→                Logout\n   232→              </button>\n   233→            </>\n   234→          ) : (\n   235→            <span>Not logged in</span>\n   236→          )}\n   237→        </div>\n   238→      </div>\n   239→    </header>\n   240→  );\n   241→}\n   242→\n   243→```\n   244→\n   245→---\n   246→\n   247→## src/contexts/AuthContext.tsx\n   248→\n   249→```tsx\n   250→import { createContext, useContext, useState, ReactNode } from 'react';\n   251→import posthog from 'posthog-js';\n   252→\n   253→interface User {\n   254→  username: string;\n   255→  burritoConsiderations: number;\n   256→}\n   257→\n   258→interface AuthContextType {\n   259→  user: User | null;\n   260→  login: (username: string, password: string) => Promise<boolean>;\n   261→  logout: () => void;\n   262→  incrementBurritoConsiderations: () => void;\n   263→}\n   264→\n   265→const AuthContext = createContext<AuthContextType | undefined>(undefined);\n   266→\n   267→const users: Map<string, User> = new Map();\n   268→\n   269→export function AuthProvider({ children }: { children: ReactNode }) {\n   270→  // Use lazy initializer to read from localStorage only once on mount\n   271→  const [user, setUser] = useState<User | null>(() => {\n   272→    if (typeof window === 'undefined') return null;\n   273→\n   274→    const storedUsername = localStorage.getItem('currentUser');\n   275→    if (storedUsername) {\n   276→      const existingUser = users.get(storedUsername);\n   277→      if (existingUser) {\n   278→        return existingUser;\n   279→      }\n   280→    }\n   281→    return null;\n   282→  });\n   283→\n   284→  const login = async (username: string, password: string): Promise<boolean> => {\n   285→    try {\n   286→      const response = await fetch('/api/auth/login', {\n   287→        method: 'POST',\n   288→        headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json' },\n   289→        body: JSON.stringify({ username, password }),\n   290→      });\n   291→\n   292→      if (response.ok) {\n   293→        const { user: userData } = await response.json();\n   294→\n   295→        // Get or create user in local map\n   296→        let localUser = users.get(username);\n   297→        if (!localUser) {\n   298→          localUser = userData as User;\n   299→          users.set(username, localUser);\n   300→        }\n   301→\n   302→        setUser(localUser);\n   303→        localStorage.setItem('currentUser', username);\n   304→\n   305→        // Identify user in PostHog using username as distinct ID\n   306→        posthog.identify(username, {\n   307→          username: username,\n   308→        });\n   309→\n   310→        // Capture login event\n   311→        posthog.capture('user_logged_in', {\n   312→          username: username,\n   313→        });\n   314→\n   315→        return true;\n   316→      }\n   317→      return false;\n   318→    } catch (error) {\n   319→      console.error('Login error:', error);\n   320→      return false;\n   321→    }\n   322→  };\n   323→\n   324→  const logout = () => {\n   325→    // Capture logout event before resetting\n   326→    posthog.capture('user_logged_out');\n   327→    posthog.reset();\n   328→\n   329→    setUser(null);\n   330→    localStorage.removeItem('currentUser');\n   331→  };\n   332→\n   333→  const incrementBurritoConsiderations = () => {\n   334→    if (user) {\n   335→      user.burritoConsiderations++;\n   336→      users.set(user.username, user);\n   337→      setUser({ ...user });\n   338→    }\n   339→  };\n   340→\n   341→  return (\n   342→    <AuthContext.Provider value={{ user, login, logout, incrementBurritoConsiderations }}>\n   343→      {children}\n   344→    </AuthContext.Provider>\n   345→  );\n   346→}\n   347→\n   348→export function useAuth() {\n   349→  const context = useContext(AuthContext);\n   350→  if (context === undefined) {\n   351→    throw new Error('useAuth must be used within an AuthProvider');\n   352→  }\n   353→  return context;\n   354→}\n   355→\n   356→```\n   357→\n   358→---\n   359→\n   360→## src/lib/posthog-server.ts\n   361→\n   362→```ts\n   363→import { PostHog } from 'posthog-node';\n   364→\n   365→let posthogClient: PostHog | null = null;\n   366→\n   367→export function getPostHogClient() {\n   368→  if (!posthogClient) {\n   369→    posthogClient = new PostHog(\n   370→      process.env.NEXT_PUBLIC_POSTHOG_KEY!,\n   371→      {\n   372→        host: process.env.NEXT_PUBLIC_POSTHOG_HOST,\n   373→        flushAt: 1,\n   374→        flushInterval: 0\n   375→      }\n   376→    );\n   377→  }\n   378→  return posthogClient;\n   379→}\n   380→\n   381→export async function shutdownPostHog() {\n   382→  if (posthogClient) {\n   383→    await posthogClient.shutdown();\n   384→  }\n   385→}\n   386→\n   387→```\n   388→\n   389→---\n   390→\n   391→## src/pages/_app.tsx\n   392→\n   393→```tsx\n   394→import \"@/styles/globals.css\";\n   395→import type { AppProps } from \"next/app\";\n   396→import { AuthProvider } from \"@/contexts/AuthContext\";\n   397→\n   398→export default function App({ Component, pageProps }: AppProps) {\n   399→  return (\n   400→    <AuthProvider>\n   401→      <Component {...pageProps} />\n   402→    </AuthProvider>\n   403→  );\n   404→}\n   405→\n   406→```\n   407→\n   408→---\n   409→\n   410→## src/pages/_document.tsx\n   411→\n   412→```tsx\n   413→import { Html, Head, Main, NextScript } from \"next/document\";\n   414→\n   415→export default function Document() {\n   416→  return (\n   417→    <Html lang=\"en\">\n   418→      <Head />\n   419→      <body>\n   420→        <Main />\n   421→        <NextScript />\n   422→      </body>\n   423→    </Html>\n   424→  );\n   425→}\n   426→\n   427→```\n   428→\n   429→---\n   430→\n   431→## src/pages/api/auth/login.ts\n   432→\n   433→```ts\n   434→import type { NextApiRequest, NextApiResponse } from 'next';\n   435→import { getPostHogClient } from '@/lib/posthog-server';\n   436→\n   437→const users = new Map<string, { username: string; burritoConsiderations: number }>();\n   438→\n   439→export default async function handler(\n   440→  req: NextApiRequest,\n   441→  res: NextApiResponse\n   442→) {\n   443→  if (req.method !== 'POST') {\n   444→    return res.status(405).json({ error: 'Method not allowed' });\n   445→  }\n   446→\n   447→  const { username, password } = req.body;\n   448→\n   449→  if (!username || !password) {\n   450→    return res.status(400).json({ error: 'Username and password required' });\n   451→  }\n   452→\n   453→  let user = users.get(username);\n   454→  const isNewUser = !user;\n   455→\n   456→  if (!user) {\n   457→    user = { username, burritoConsiderations: 0 };\n   458→    users.set(username, user);\n   459→  }\n   460→\n   461→  // Capture server-side login event\n   462→  const posthog = getPostHogClient();\n   463→  posthog.capture({\n   464→    distinctId: username,\n   465→    event: 'server_login',\n   466→    properties: {\n   467→      username: username,\n   468→      isNewUser: isNewUser,\n   469→      source: 'api'\n   470→    }\n   471→  });\n   472→\n   473→  // Identify user on server side\n   474→  posthog.identify({\n   475→    distinctId: username,\n   476→    properties: {\n   477→      username: username,\n   478→      createdAt: isNewUser ? new Date().toISOString() : undefined\n   479→    }\n   480→  });\n   481→\n   482→  return res.status(200).json({ success: true, user });\n   483→}\n   484→\n   485→```\n   486→\n   487→---\n   488→\n   489→## src/pages/api/hello.ts\n   490→\n   491→```ts\n   492→// Next.js API route support: https://nextjs.org/docs/api-routes/introduction\n   493→import type { NextApiRequest, NextApiResponse } from \"next\";\n   494→\n   495→type Data = {\n   496→  name: string;\n   497→};\n   498→\n   499→export default function handler(\n   500→  req: NextApiRequest,\n   501→  res: NextApiResponse<Data>,\n   502→) {\n   503→  res.status(200).json({ name: \"John Doe\" });\n   504→}\n   505→\n   506→```\n   507→\n   508→---\n   509→\n   510→## src/pages/burrito.tsx\n   511→\n   512→```tsx\n   513→import { useState } from 'react';\n   514→import Head from 'next/head';\n   515→import { useRouter } from 'next/router';\n   516→import posthog from 'posthog-js';\n   517→import { useAuth } from '@/contexts/AuthContext';\n   518→import Header from '@/components/Header';\n   519→\n   520→export default function BurritoPage() {\n   521→  const { user, incrementBurritoConsiderations } = useAuth();\n   522→  const router = useRouter();\n   523→  const [hasConsidered, setHasConsidered] = useState(false);\n   524→\n   525→  // Redirect to home if not logged in\n   526→  if (!user) {\n   527→    router.push('/');\n   528→    return null;\n   529→  }\n   530→\n   531→  const handleConsideration = () => {\n   532→    incrementBurritoConsiderations();\n   533→    setHasConsidered(true);\n   534→    setTimeout(() => setHasConsidered(false), 2000);\n   535→\n   536→    // Capture burrito consideration event\n   537→    posthog.capture('burrito_considered', {\n   538→      total_considerations: user.burritoConsiderations + 1,\n   539→      username: user.username,\n   540→    });\n   541→  };\n   542→\n   543→  return (\n   544→    <>\n   545→      <Head>\n   546→        <title>Burrito Consideration - Burrito Consideration App</title>\n   547→        <meta name=\"description\" content=\"Consider the potential of burritos\" />\n   548→        <meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1\" />\n   549→        <link rel=\"icon\" href=\"/favicon.ico\" />\n   550→      </Head>\n   551→      <Header />\n   552→      <main>\n   553→        <div className=\"container\">\n   554→          <h1>Burrito consideration zone</h1>\n   555→          <p>Take a moment to truly consider the potential of burritos.</p>\n   556→\n   557→          <div style={{ textAlign: 'center' }}>\n   558→            <button\n   559→              onClick={handleConsideration}\n   560→              className=\"btn-burrito\"\n   561→            >\n   562→              I have considered the burrito potential\n   563→            </button>\n   564→\n   565→            {hasConsidered && (\n   566→              <p className=\"success\">\n   567→                Thank you for your consideration! Count: {user.burritoConsiderations}\n   568→              </p>\n   569→            )}\n   570→          </div>\n   571→\n   572→          <div className=\"stats\">\n   573→            <h3>Consideration stats</h3>\n   574→            <p>Total considerations: {user.burritoConsiderations}</p>\n   575→          </div>\n   576→        </div>\n   577→      </main>\n   578→    </>\n   579→  );\n   580→}\n   581→\n   582→```\n   583→\n   584→---\n   585→\n   586→## src/pages/index.tsx\n   587→\n   588→```tsx\n   589→import { useState } from 'react';\n   590→import Head from 'next/head';\n   591→import { useAuth } from '@/contexts/AuthContext';\n   592→import Header from '@/components/Header';\n   593→\n   594→export default function Home() {\n   595→  const { user, login } = useAuth();\n   596→  const [username, setUsername] = useState('');\n   597→  const [password, setPassword] = useState('');\n   598→  const [error, setError] = useState('');\n   599→\n   600→  const handleSubmit = async (e: React.FormEvent) => {\n   601→    e.preventDefault();\n   602→    setError('');\n   603→\n   604→    try {\n   605→      const success = await login(username, password);\n   606→      if (success) {\n   607→        setUsername('');\n   608→        setPassword('');\n   609→      } else {\n   610→        setError('Please provide both username and password');\n   611→      }\n   612→    } catch (err) {\n   613→      console.error('Login failed:', err);\n   614→      setError('An error occurred during login');\n   615→    }\n   616→  };\n   617→\n   618→  return (\n   619→    <>\n   620→      <Head>\n   621→        <title>Burrito Consideration App</title>\n   622→        <meta name=\"description\" content=\"Consider the potential of burritos\" />\n   623→        <meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1\" />\n   624→        <link rel=\"icon\" href=\"/favicon.ico\" />\n   625→      </Head>\n   626→      <Header />\n   627→      <main>\n   628→        {user ? (\n   629→          <div className=\"container\">\n   630→            <h1>Welcome back, {user.username}!</h1>\n   631→            <p>You are now logged in. Feel free to explore:</p>\n   632→            <ul>\n   633→              <li>Consider the potential of burritos</li>\n   634→              <li>View your profile and statistics</li>\n   635→            </ul>\n   636→          </div>\n   637→        ) : (\n   638→          <div className=\"container\">\n   639→            <h1>Welcome to Burrito Consideration App</h1>\n   640→            <p>Please sign in to begin your burrito journey</p>\n   641→\n   642→            <form onSubmit={handleSubmit} className=\"form\">\n   643→              <div className=\"form-group\">\n   644→                <label htmlFor=\"username\">Username:</label>\n   645→                <input\n   646→                  type=\"text\"\n   647→                  id=\"username\"\n   648→                  value={username}\n   649→                  onChange={(e) => setUsername(e.target.value)}\n   650→                  placeholder=\"Enter any username\"\n   651→                />\n   652→              </div>\n   653→\n   654→              <div className=\"form-group\">\n   655→                <label htmlFor=\"password\">Password:</label>\n   656→                <input\n   657→                  type=\"password\"\n   658→                  id=\"password\"\n   659→                  value={password}\n   660→                  onChange={(e) => setPassword(e.target.value)}\n   661→                  placeholder=\"Enter any password\"\n   662→                />\n   663→              </div>\n   664→\n   665→              {error && <p className=\"error\">{error}</p>}\n   666→\n   667→              <button type=\"submit\" className=\"btn-primary\">Sign In</button>\n   668→            </form>\n   669→\n   670→            <p className=\"note\">\n   671→              Note: This is a demo app. Use any username and password to sign in.\n   672→            </p>\n   673→          </div>\n   674→        )}\n   675→      </main>\n   676→    </>\n   677→  );\n   678→}\n   679→\n   680→```\n   681→\n   682→---\n   683→\n   684→## src/pages/profile.tsx\n   685→\n   686→```tsx\n   687→import Head from 'next/head';\n   688→import { useRouter } from 'next/router';\n   689→import posthog from 'posthog-js';\n   690→import { useAuth } from '@/contexts/AuthContext';\n   691→import Header from '@/components/Header';\n   692→\n   693→export default function ProfilePage() {\n   694→  const { user } = useAuth();\n   695→  const router = useRouter();\n   696→\n   697→  // Redirect to home if not logged in\n   698→  if (!user) {\n   699→    router.push('/');\n   700→    return null;\n   701→  }\n   702→\n   703→  const triggerTestError = () => {\n   704→    try {\n   705→      throw new Error('Test error for PostHog error tracking');\n   706→    } catch (err) {\n   707→      posthog.captureException(err);\n   708→      console.error('Captured error:', err);\n   709→      alert('Error captured and sent to PostHog!');\n   710→    }\n   711→  };\n   712→\n   713→  return (\n   714→    <>\n   715→      <Head>\n   716→        <title>Profile - Burrito Consideration App</title>\n   717→        <meta name=\"description\" content=\"Your burrito consideration profile\" />\n   718→        <meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1\" />\n   719→        <link rel=\"icon\" href=\"/favicon.ico\" />\n   720→      </Head>\n   721→      <Header />\n   722→      <main>\n   723→        <div className=\"container\">\n   724→          <h1>User Profile</h1>\n   725→\n   726→          <div className=\"stats\">\n   727→            <h2>Your Information</h2>\n   728→            <p><strong>Username:</strong> {user.username}</p>\n   729→            <p><strong>Burrito Considerations:</strong> {user.burritoConsiderations}</p>\n   730→          </div>\n   731→\n   732→          <div style={{ marginTop: '2rem' }}>\n   733→            <button onClick={triggerTestError} className=\"btn-primary\" style={{ backgroundColor: '#dc3545' }}>\n   734→              Trigger Test Error (for PostHog)\n   735→            </button>\n   736→          </div>\n   737→\n   738→          <div style={{ marginTop: '2rem' }}>\n   739→            <h3>Your Burrito Journey</h3>\n   740→            {user.burritoConsiderations === 0 ? (\n   741→              <p>You haven&apos;t considered any burritos yet. Visit the Burrito Consideration page to start!</p>\n   742→            ) : user.burritoConsiderations === 1 ? (\n   743→              <p>You&apos;ve considered the burrito potential once. Keep going!</p>\n   744→            ) : user.burritoConsiderations < 5 ? (\n   745→              <p>You&apos;re getting the hang of burrito consideration!</p>\n   746→            ) : user.burritoConsiderations < 10 ? (\n   747→              <p>You&apos;re becoming a burrito consideration expert!</p>\n   748→            ) : (\n   749→              <p>You are a true burrito consideration master! 🌯</p>\n   750→            )}\n   751→          </div>\n   752→        </div>\n   753→      </main>\n   754→    </>\n   755→  );\n   756→}\n   757→\n   758→```\n   759→\n   760→---\n   761→\n   762→\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"
      }
    ]
